## 8. Risks that could shift priorities

| Risk | If it materialises | Priority shift |
|---|---|---|
| A target customer requires weekly/fortnightly payroll | Multi-frequency becomes a sales blocker | **G11 moves P2 → P0/P1** |
| Regulated jurisdiction becomes primary market | Statutory compliance becomes existential | **G1 effort increases; consider localisation partner** |
| Biometric hardware already deployed in production | Manual re-keying is a live pain point | **G5 moves P1 → P0** |
| Finance team is small and cannot handle manual reconciliation | Ledger becomes urgent | **G2 moves earlier within P0** |
| Employee count grows past ~200 | Effective dating and lifecycle documents become critical for arrears | **G8 confirmed as P0; G6 moved earlier in P1** |
| Loan programmes are a customer requirement | Advances-lite is insufficient | **G3 moves P1 → P0** |
| Expense reimbursements are high-volume | Manual processing cost is high | **G7 moves P2 → P1** |
| Mobile-first workforce | SPA-only access is a blocker | **G14 moves P3 → P1** |

