## 9. Acceptance criteria per tier

### P0 acceptance

- A salary revision creates a **new effective-dated assignment** without overwriting history (G8).
- Statutory deductions are computed **entirely from DB configuration**; a super-admin can create, version, preview, publish, and archive rules **without a code deploy** (G1).
- Payroll lock posts a **balanced journal entry** to a general ledger, reconcilable via trial balance (G2).
- All three tiers are covered by automated tests at the existing coverage gate.

### P1 acceptance

- An employee can repay a **loan with interest** through payroll deductions over a multi-month schedule (G3).
- Hourly/contractor employees can be paid **from recorded timesheet hours** (G4).
- Attendance flows **from biometric devices** into payroll; LWP-dependent components compute without manual intervention (G5).
- A promotion or transfer generates an **effective-dated lifecycle document** with full audit trail (G6).

### P2 acceptance

- Employees can submit **expense claims** with receipts; approval routes through multi-level workflow; claims post to the ledger (G7).
- Employees can **declare tax investments** and see projected tax impact (G10).
- Payroll supports **weekly, fortnightly, and off-cycle** runs with correct proration and YTD across frequencies (G11).
- Reviews are linked to **goals and KRAs** (G9).

### P3 acceptance

- Bank payment files can be generated in **at least one local format** and reconciled on payment (G12).
- Onboarding templates can be scoped by **department, designation, or grade** (G13).
- A **mobile/PWA client** provides core self-service (G14).

